 34SI c  2019Li41: {+34}Mg and {+34}Al ions were produced via fragmentation     
 34SI2c  reactions induced by a 1.4-GeV pulsed proton beam from the Proton      
 34SI3c  Synchrotron Booster on a UC{-x} target at CERN-ISOLDE. The atoms that  
 34SI4c  diffused out of the target matrix were selectively laser ionized using 
 34SI5c  the resonance ionization laser ion source (RILIS) and accelerated to 40
 34SI6c  keV. A=34 nuclei were selected by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator 
 34SI7c  and implanted onto a movable tape located at the center of the ISOLDE  
 34SI8c  Decay station. The {+34}Mg beam rate is 700 pps {I1} and the {+34}Al   
 34SI9c  beam rate is 800 pps {I1}, both with purities of >99%. |b particles    
 34SIAc  were detected using a 3-cm-thick NE102 plastic scintillator with an    
 34SIBc  efficiency of 90% {I5}. |g rays were detected using five HPGe clover   
 34SICc  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |b|g|g-coin, and              
 34SIDc  |be{++}/e{+-}coin. Deduced levels, isomer, J, |p, decay branching      
 34SIEc  ratios, log {Ift}, T{-1/2} and %|b{+-}n of parent, and configuration   
 34SIFc  mixings. Comparisons with large-scale shell-model calculations using   
 34SIGc  the SDPF-U-MIX interaction.                                            
 34SI c  2017Ha23, 2017Ha34: a 69.2-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was        
 34SI2c  produced by the Sector Focusing Cyclotron and Separated Sector         
 34SI3c  Cyclotron at the Heavy Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL). The   
 34SI4c  secondary beam containing {+34}Al was produced via the projectile      
 34SI5c  fragmentation of {+40}Ca impinging on a 182.6-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target  
 34SI6c  and was selected using |DE-tof-B|r by the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in 
 34SI7c  Lanzhou (RIBLL). The secondary beam ions were transported into a target
 34SI8c  chamber filled with low-temperature nitrogen and implanted into a      
 34SI9c  1500-|mm-thick DSSD sandwiched between two 3000-|mm-thick plastic      
 34SIAc  scintillators for beam diagnostics and veto, respectively. |g rays were
 34SIBc  detected using two Ge clover detectors. The fast timing signals of the 
 34SICc  |g rays were provided by a lanthanum bromide (LaBr{-3}) detector.      
 34SIDc  Neutrons were detected using two plastic scintillator arrays. Measured 
 34SIEc  implant-|b correlation, E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, and |bn-coin.  
 34SIFc  Deduced levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, parent       
 34SIGc  {+34}Al and {+34}Al isomer T{-1/2}. Comparisons with shell-model       
 34SIHc  calculations using Gogny D1S and SDPF-M interactions. Also see 2019Wa38
 34SIIc  for the same experiment with {+35}Al |b-delayed neutron data.          
 34SI c  2012Ro25: a 600-pps, 93% pure {+34}Al secondary beam was produced via  
 34SI2c  the projectile fragmentation of a 77.5-MeV/nucleon {+36}S primary beam 
 34SI3c  on a 240-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target and selected by the LISE3 spectrometer
 34SI4c  at GANIL. {+34}Al ions were implanted into a 50-|mm Kapton foil in a   
 34SI5c  beam-on (120 ms)/beam-off (300 ms) mode. Electrons and positrons were  
 34SI6c  detected using four |DE-E telescopes, each consisting of a 1-mm-thick  
 34SI7c  Si detector and a 4.5-mm-thick Si(Li) detector. |g rays were detected  
 34SI8c  using two Ge clover detectors of the EXOGAM array. Measured E|b,       
 34SI9c  Ee{++}, Ee{+-}, E|g, |b|g-coin, and |be{++}/e{+-}coin. Deduced {+34}Al 
 34SIAc  g.s. and isomer T{-1/2}, {+34}Si levels, J, |p, transition strengths,  
 34SIBc  and configuration mixing. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.   
 34SICc  Earlier measurements at GANIL: 1988Mu08, 1986Du07.                     
 34SI c  2001Nu01: a {+34}Al secondary beam at 30 pps was produced via the      
 34SI2c  fragmentation of a UC target with 1-GeV protons at ISOLDE, CERN with   
 34SI3c  subsequent surface-ionization and mass separation. {+34}Al ions were   
 34SI4c  collected onto a moving tape. |b particles were detected using a thin  
 34SI5c  cylindrical plastic scintillator, |g rays were detected using two Ge   
 34SI6c  detectors, and neutrons were detected using eight low-threshold plastic
 34SI7c  scintillators. Measured E|g, I|g, E{-n}, I{-n}, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin,  
 34SI8c  |bn-coin. Deduced the decay scheme consisting of {+33}Si and {+34}Si   
 34SI9c  levels, {+34}Al T{-1/2}, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, and        
 34SIAc  |b-delayed neutron emission probability. Comparisons with shell-model  
 34SIBc  calculations. Earlier measurement at ISOLDE: 1989Ba50.                 
 34SI c  The decay scheme is considered incomplete due to a large gap of about  
 34SI2c  10.8 MeV between the highest observed level at E=6227 and Q(|b{+-})    
 34SI3c  value=16994.1 {I23} (2021Wa16). There may be missing transitions from  
 34SI4c  unobserved levels in the gap.                                          
 34SI cB IB,LOGFT$|b-feeding intensity is from |g-ray intensity balance at each 
 34SI2cB level. Quoted I|b{+-} values are considered upper limits due to the    
 34SI3cB incomplete decay scheme, and the associated log {Ift} values are       
 34SI4cB considered lower limits.                                               
