 34SI2cN 100-%|b{+-}n-%I|b{+-}(g.s.), where %|b{+-}n=22 {I5} from the Adopted   
 34SI3cN Levels of {+34}Al (originally from 2019Li41) and %I|b{+-}(g.s.)=0. The 
 34SI4cN deduced normalization factor may be considered an upper limit due to   
 34SI5cN potential missing |g transitions from unobserved levels in the gap to  
 34SI6cN the ground state. The original normalization factor is 0.61 {I6} in    
 34SI7cN 2019Li41. 2019Li41 states that the numbers of implanted {+34}Mg and    
 34SI8cN {+34}Al nuclei are derived from singles |g-ray spectra, using the      
 34SI9cN transitions corresponding to the last populated daughters in the decay 
 34SIAcN chains.                                                                
